 {
  "slug": "glossary",
  "title": "Glossary",
  "section": "Reference",
  "order": 96,
  "summary": "Short definitions of the words used across Agent Studio.",
  "routes": [],
  "tags": [
   "glossary",
   "terms",
   "definitions",
   "words",
   "acronyms",
   "a2a",
   "acp",
   "mcp",
   "rag",
   "ag-ui",
   "ocsf",
   "otlp",
   "spiffe"
  ],
  "intro": "**A2A** (agent to agent). An open way for agents on different servers to talk. See [API and A2A](doc:api-and-a2a).\n\n**ACP** (Agent Client Protocol). How Agent Studio drives outside coding agents. See [External agents](doc:external-agents).\n\n**Agent.** A model with instructions, tools and a job. See [Agents](doc:agents).\n\n**AG-UI.** How an agent shows rich answers and streams its work. See [Rich answers](doc:rich-answers).\n\n**AI-BOM.** A bill of materials for an AI system, in CycloneDX format. See [AI-BOM](doc:ai-bom).\n\n**Artifact.** A file or result an agent produced. See [Artifacts](doc:artifacts).\n\n**Auto mode.** Picking a model for each message automatically. See [Chat](doc:chat).\n\n**Barge-in.** Talking over the assistant to interrupt it. See [Live mode](doc:live-mode).\n\n**Canvas.** A document, code or table you edit with an agent. See [Canvas](doc:canvas).\n\n**Context window.** How much text a model can keep in mind at once, counted in tokens (about three-quarters of a word each).\n\n**d1.** A small decision model on this PC that answers quick \"which one?\" or \"yes or no?\" questions for free.\n\n**Embedding.** Turning text into numbers so it can be searched by meaning. See [Knowledge](doc:knowledge).\n\n**Guardrail.** A check on what goes into a model, comes out, or what tools do. See [Guardrails](doc:guardrails).\n\n**MCP** (Model Context Protocol). The add-on standard for giving agents tools. See [MCP servers](doc:mcp-servers).\n\n**Ollama.** Free software that runs AI models on your own PC.\n\n**OCSF.** A standard format for security events. See [Telemetry](doc:telemetry).\n\n**OTLP / OpenTelemetry.** A standard format for traces. See [Telemetry](doc:telemetry).\n\n**Provider.** The company or program a model comes from. See [Model providers](doc:providers).\n\n**RAG** (retrieval augmented generation). Looking things up in your documents before answering. See [Knowledge](doc:knowledge).\n\n**Sandbox.** A locked Docker box where commands run.\n\n**Skill.** A saved how-to guide an agent reads when needed. See [Skills](doc:skills).\n\n**SPIFFE.** A naming scheme for workload identity, used for agent IDs. See [Guardrails and identity](doc:guardrails).\n\n**Spend limit.** The most a provider may cost you, checked before every request. See [Billing and limits](doc:billing-and-limits).\n\n**Sub-agent.** An agent another agent hands work to. See [Agents](doc:agents).\n\n**Token.** A small piece of text a model reads or writes. Also, a secret that grants access; never paste one into a chat.\n\n**Workflow.** Boxes and arrows that run steps in order. See [Workflows](doc:workflows).\n\n**Workspace.** The one folder agents may read and change.",
  "sections": [],
  "shots": [],
  "words": 364
 }
